## Generators

Each starts a new map {% own /%}.

{% card title="Random rooms" id="rooms" kind="Generator" %}
Scatter rectangles over a solid map, keep the ones that don’t overlap, and join them with corridors {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s47" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s48" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s49" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s50" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s51" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-slides/pdf#p5" /%}.

Stage `rooms`. The talk’s demo: `c01-rooms`.

{% part title="The rule" %}
1. **Repeat 20 times** {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L21" /%}:
   1. pick a random rectangle {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L22-L27" /%};
   2. if it overlaps or touches a room already placed, discard it {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L28-L53" /%};
   3. otherwise carve it as a room {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L40-L46" /%}.
2. Sort the rooms by their left edge {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L57" /%}.
3. Join each room to the one before it, center to center {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L67-L78" /%}:
   - a corridor of two runs, one across and one up or down {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L72-L76" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L85-L101" /%};
   - a coin flip picks which run comes first {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L71-L76" /%}.

{% figure src="assets/rules/rooms-join-light.png" dark="assets/rules/rooms-join-dark.png" alt="A solid map with two rooms. A corridor runs right from the first room’s center, then down into the second room’s center. A third rectangle that touches the second room is marked as rejected." caption="A rectangle that touches a room is discarded (small squares). Two rooms are joined center to center by one run across and one down (marked tiles)." /%}

- **Talk says:** anyone who has done a roguelike development tutorial has seen this one {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s45" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s46" /%}.
- **Talk says:** keep adding rooms until there are enough by your own criteria {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s50" /%}.
- **Demo:** a fixed 20 attempts. A rectangle that overlaps is discarded without another try {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L20-L54" /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="Step-through" %}
{% interactive id="lab" caption="Step through Random rooms: seed 1, 80 by 50 tiles. Change the seed or a control and the map is built again." params={mode: "card", stage: "rooms", demos: ["c01-rooms"]} %}
{% steps %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c01-0001-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c01-0001-dark.png" alt="Random rooms, seed 1: the map at step 1 of 30." key="rooms.add" at=1 of=30 %}
**Room:** a random rectangle that overlaps or touches no room placed so far, carved as a room {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L22-L46" /%}. Room {% value %}1{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c01-0008-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c01-0008-dark.png" alt="Random rooms, seed 1: the map at step 8 of 30." key="rooms.discard" at=8 of=30 %}
**Discarded:** this rectangle overlaps or touches a room already placed {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L22-L53" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s54" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s55" /%}. Rooms so far: {% value %}7{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c01-0014-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c01-0014-dark.png" alt="Random rooms, seed 1: the map at step 14 of 30." key="rooms.add" at=14 of=30 %}
**Room:** a random rectangle that overlaps or touches no room placed so far, carved as a room {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L22-L46" /%}. Room {% value %}10{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c01-0021-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c01-0021-dark.png" alt="Random rooms, seed 1: the map at step 21 of 30." key="rooms.sort" at=21 of=30 %}
**Sort:** the rooms, by their left edge: the order they are joined in {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L57-L69" /%}. Rooms to join: {% value %}10{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c01-0022-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c01-0022-dark.png" alt="Random rooms, seed 1: the map at step 22 of 30." key="rooms.corridor" at=22 of=30 %}
**Corridor:** from this room’s center to the center of the room before it. One run across and one up or down; a coin flip picks which comes first {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L67-L78" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L85-L101" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s57" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s58" /%}. Corridor {% value %}1{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c01-0030-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c01-0030-dark.png" alt="Random rooms, seed 1: the map at step 30 of 30." key="rooms.corridor" at=30 of=30 %}
**Corridor:** from this room’s center to the center of the room before it. One run across and one up or down; a coin flip picks which comes first {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L67-L78" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L85-L101" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s57" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s58" /%}. Corridor {% value %}9{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% /steps %}

On the command line: `map-lab build recipes/c01-rooms.json`.
{% /interactive %}
{% /part %}

{% part title="Controls" %}
- `attempts` (1 to 500; the talk’s: `20`) {% own /%}. Rectangles tried. The demo: a fixed 20, and a discarded one is not tried again {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L20-L54" /%}.
- `min_size` (1 to 30; the talk’s: `2`) {% own /%}. Smallest value a room’s width and height are drawn from {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L22-L27" /%}. A room covers 1 tile more than the value each way: the demo’s rectangle type includes both of its ends {% own /%}.
- `max_size` (1 to 30; the talk’s: `9`) {% own /%}. Largest value they are drawn from. The demo writes 10 as the upper end, which its random call leaves out {% own /%}.
{% /part %}

