{% card title="Binary space partition rooms" id="bsp" kind="Generator" %}
Rooms placed in ever-smaller parts of the map, so they come out better spaced than random rooms {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s61" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s62" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s63" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s64" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-slides/pdf#p7" /%}.

Stage `bsp`. The talk’s demo: `c02-bsprooms`.

{% part title="The rule" %}
1. Start a list with one rectangle inside the map’s edge, and that rectangle’s four quarters {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L24-L29" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L87-L111" /%}.
2. **Repeat 240 times** {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L41-L54" /%}:
   1. pick any rectangle on the list {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L43" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L114-L120" /%};
   2. try a room near its top-left corner {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L44" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L122-L136" /%};
   3. if every tile within 2 of the room is solid and inside the map’s outer ring, carve the room {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L45-L49" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L138-L174" /%};
   4. then add the four quarters of the rectangle it came from to the list {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L50" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L86-L112" /%}.
3. Sort the rooms by their left edge, and join each to the one before it with a corridor {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L57-L78" /%}.

{% figure src="assets/rules/bsp-quarters-light.png" dark="assets/rules/bsp-quarters-dark.png" alt="A rectangle cut into four quarters, each tinted differently. A small room sits near the top-left corner of the first quarter, and another near the top-left corner of the last." caption="The demo’s list holds a rectangle’s four quarters (tinted). A room is tried near the top-left corner of whichever rectangle is picked." /%}

- **Talk says:** halve the map, then each half, until a piece is about the size of a room {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s66" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s67" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s68" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s69" /%}.
- **Demo:** looser. It cuts into quarters, keeps every rectangle it has cut on its list, and quarters a rectangle again each time a room lands in it {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L41-L55" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L86-L121" /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="Step-through" %}
{% interactive id="lab" caption="Step through BSP rooms: seed 1, 80 by 50 tiles. Change the seed or a control and the map is built again." params={mode: "card", stage: "bsp", demos: ["c02-bsprooms"]} %}
{% steps %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c02-0001-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c02-0001-dark.png" alt="BSP rooms, seed 1: the map at step 1 of 45." key="bsp.subdivide" at=1 of=45 %}
**The list:** it starts with one rectangle inside the map’s edge, and that rectangle’s four quarters {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L24-L29" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L87-L111" /%}. Quarters shown: {% value %}0{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c02-0006-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c02-0006-dark.png" alt="BSP rooms, seed 1: the map at step 6 of 45." key="bsp.add" at=6 of=45 %}
**Attempt:** pick any rectangle on the list and try a room near its top-left corner {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L43-L44" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L114-L136" /%}. The room is carved only if every tile within 2 of it is still solid and inside the map’s outer ring. Then the rectangle it came from is quartered again {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L45-L52" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L86-L112" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L138-L174" /%}. Room {% value %}1{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c02-0025-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c02-0025-dark.png" alt="BSP rooms, seed 1: the map at step 25 of 45." key="bsp.add" at=25 of=45 %}
**Attempt:** pick any rectangle on the list and try a room near its top-left corner {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L43-L44" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L114-L136" /%}. The room is carved only if every tile within 2 of it is still solid and inside the map’s outer ring. Then the rectangle it came from is quartered again {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L45-L52" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L86-L112" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L138-L174" /%}. Room {% value %}20{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c02-0026-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c02-0026-dark.png" alt="BSP rooms, seed 1: the map at step 26 of 45." key="rooms.sort" at=26 of=45 %}
**Sort:** the rooms, by their left edge: the order they are joined in {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L57-L69" /%}. Rooms to join: {% value %}20{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c02-0027-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c02-0027-dark.png" alt="BSP rooms, seed 1: the map at step 27 of 45." key="rooms.corridor" at=27 of=45 %}
**Corridor:** from this room’s center to the center of the room before it. One run across and one up or down; a coin flip picks which comes first {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L67-L78" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L85-L101" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s57" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s58" /%}. Corridor {% value %}1{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c02-0045-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c02-0045-dark.png" alt="BSP rooms, seed 1: the map at step 45 of 45." key="rooms.corridor" at=45 of=45 %}
**Corridor:** from this room’s center to the center of the room before it. One run across and one up or down; a coin flip picks which comes first {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L67-L78" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L85-L101" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s57" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s58" /%}. Corridor {% value %}19{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% /steps %}

On the command line: `map-lab build recipes/c02-bsprooms.json`.
{% /interactive %}
{% /part %}

{% part title="Controls" %}
- `attempts` (1 to 5,000; the talk’s: `240`) {% own /%}. Times a rectangle is picked and a room tried. The demo’s counter goes up on every attempt, whether or not the room fits {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L41-L55" /%}.
{% /part %}

