{% card title="Cellular automata" id="cellular" kind="Generator" %}
Random noise, with cell life rules applied to every tile again and again, until a natural-looking map comes out of it {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s73" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s74" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s83" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s84" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-slides/pdf#p9" /%}.

Stage `cellular`. The talk’s demo: `c03-cellular`.

{% part title="The rule" %}
1. **Noise:** every tile, the map’s edge included, starts as wall with a set chance, else as floor. The demo: 55% {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c03-cellular/src/main.rs#L19-L29" /%}.
2. **Repeat 10 times,** for every tile inside the map’s outer ring at once {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c03-cellular/src/main.rs#L31-L34" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c03-cellular/src/main.rs#L56-L70" /%}:
   1. count the walls among the tile’s 8 neighbors, in a copy of the map made before the pass {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c03-cellular/src/main.rs#L40-L60" /%};
   2. 0 walls: the tile becomes wall {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c03-cellular/src/main.rs#L61-L66" /%};
   3. 1 to 4 walls: the tile becomes floor {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c03-cellular/src/main.rs#L61-L66" /%};
   4. 5 or more walls: the tile becomes wall {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c03-cellular/src/main.rs#L61-L66" /%}.

{% figure src="assets/rules/cellular-count-light.png" dark="assets/rules/cellular-count-dark.png" alt="Three tiles, each with its eight neighbors, before a pass and after it. The first has no wall among its neighbors and becomes wall. The second has two and becomes floor. The third has five and becomes wall." caption="A tile’s count of walls among its 8 neighbors (top) decides what it becomes (bottom): 0, wall; 1 to 4, floor; 5 or more, wall. Only the middle tile’s change is drawn." /%}

- **Talk says:** no neighbors, a wall; 1 to 4, empty; 5 or more, a wall {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s80" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s81" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s82" /%}.
- **Demo:** the neighbors it counts are walls, and a tile’s own state plays no part in what it becomes {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c03-cellular/src/main.rs#L40-L70" /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="Step-through" %}
{% interactive id="lab" caption="Step through Cellular automata: seed 1, 80 by 50 tiles. Change the seed or a control and the map is built again." params={mode: "card", stage: "cellular", demos: ["c03-cellular"]} %}
{% steps %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c03-0001-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c03-0001-dark.png" alt="Cellular automata, seed 1: the map at step 1 of 11." key="cellular.noise" at=1 of=11 %}
**Noise:** every tile, the map’s edge included, starts as wall with a {% value %}55{% /value %}% chance, else as floor {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c03-cellular/src/main.rs#L19-L29" /%}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c03-0002-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c03-0002-dark.png" alt="Cellular automata, seed 1: the map at step 2 of 11." key="cellular.iterate" at=2 of=11 %}
**A pass:** every tile inside the map’s outer ring counts the walls among its 8 neighbors, in a copy of the map made before the pass {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c03-cellular/src/main.rs#L40-L70" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s79" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s80" /%}. 5 or more, or none: wall. 1 to 4: floor {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c03-cellular/src/main.rs#L61-L66" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s81" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s82" /%}. Pass {% value %}1{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c03-0006-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c03-0006-dark.png" alt="Cellular automata, seed 1: the map at step 6 of 11." key="cellular.iterate" at=6 of=11 %}
**A pass:** every tile inside the map’s outer ring counts the walls among its 8 neighbors, in a copy of the map made before the pass {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c03-cellular/src/main.rs#L40-L70" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s79" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s80" /%}. 5 or more, or none: wall. 1 to 4: floor {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c03-cellular/src/main.rs#L61-L66" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s81" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s82" /%}. Pass {% value %}5{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c03-0011-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c03-0011-dark.png" alt="Cellular automata, seed 1: the map at step 11 of 11." key="cellular.iterate" at=11 of=11 %}
**A pass:** every tile inside the map’s outer ring counts the walls among its 8 neighbors, in a copy of the map made before the pass {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c03-cellular/src/main.rs#L40-L70" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s79" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s80" /%}. 5 or more, or none: wall. 1 to 4: floor {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c03-cellular/src/main.rs#L61-L66" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s81" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s82" /%}. Pass {% value %}10{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% /steps %}

On the command line: `map-lab build recipes/c03-cellular.json`.
{% /interactive %}
{% /part %}

{% part title="Controls" %}
- `wall_percent` (0 to 100; the talk’s: `55`) {% own /%}. Chance each tile starts as wall {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c03-cellular/src/main.rs#L19-L29" /%}.
- `iterations` (0 to 100; the talk’s: `10`) {% own /%}. Times the rule is applied to the whole map {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c03-cellular/src/main.rs#L31-L34" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c03-cellular/src/main.rs#L56-L70" /%}.
{% /part %}

