- **Talk says:** guaranteed to be contiguous {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s99" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s100" /%}.
- **Drunkard’s walk:** holds. 1 region on every seed {% own-run values="c04.regions.max" /%}.
- **Passages:** wide. Corridor ratio 0.053 at the median, vs cellular automata’s 0.131 {% own-run values="c04.corridor_ratio.median c03.corridor_ratio.median" /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="Failures" %}
No seed from 0 to 199 fails any of [our criteria](#failure-criteria) {% own-run values="list.fails.drunkard" /%}.

- **No cap in the talk’s code:** its loop of diggers ends only when the open share is reached {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c04-drunkard/src/main.rs#L25-L48" /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="Combinations" %}
None of the talk’s demos runs it with another stage {% own /%}.

- **Talk’s use:** limestone caverns and similar {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s100" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s101" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s102" /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="Faithfulness" %}
Our stage against the talk’s own code, each run on seeds 0 to 199 and [measured the same way](#faithfulness-to-the-talks-code) {% own-run values="list.checked.drunkard" /%}:

- `c04-drunkard`: 8 of 8 traits consistent with the talk’s own code.
{% /part %}

{% /card %}

{% card title="Diffusion-limited aggregation" id="dla" kind="Generator" %}
Dig a small open seed, then start particles on random tiles. Each travels until it reaches open floor, and digs the last solid tile it stood on {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c05-dla/src/main.rs#L19-L82" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s103" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s104" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s105" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s106" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s107" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s108" /%}.

Stage `dla`. The talk’s demos: `c05-dla`, `c06-dla-attractor`, `c07-dla-symmetry`.

{% part title="The rule" %}
1. **Seed:** dig a plus of five tiles at the center of a solid map {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c05-dla/src/main.rs#L19-L40" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s103" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s104" /%}.
2. **Until a third of the map is open** {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c05-dla/src/main.rs#L43" /%}:
   1. start a particle on a random tile {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c05-dla/src/main.rs#L49-L52" /%};
   2. move it until it stands on open floor {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c05-dla/src/main.rs#L53-L80" /%};
   3. dig the last solid tile it stood on {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c05-dla/src/main.rs#L53-L82" /%}.

The talk gives three versions: the simple one, a central attractor, and the attractor with a symmetry applied {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s103" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s104" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s111" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s112" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s115" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s116" /%}. In its demos they differ in step 2 {% own /%}:

{% table label="How a particle travels, by version" rowheads=true %}
* Version
* The particle moves
* It digs
---
* `walk` (c05)
* one random step at a time {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c05-dla/src/main.rs#L55-L80" /%}
* the last solid tile it stood on {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c05-dla/src/main.rs#L55-L82" /%}
---
* `attractor` (c06)
* along a straight line to the center {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c06-dla-attractor/src/main.rs#L56-L66" /%}
* the last solid tile it stood on {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c06-dla-attractor/src/main.rs#L62-L68" /%}
---
* `symmetric` (c07)
* along a straight line to the center {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c07-dla-symmetry/src/main.rs#L56-L67" /%}
* that tile and its mirror image across the middle column {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c07-dla-symmetry/src/main.rs#L62-L77" /%}
{% /table %}

{% figure src="assets/rules/dla-walk-light.png" dark="assets/rules/dla-walk-dark.png" alt="A solid map with a plus of five open tiles at its center. A particle starts at the top left and takes four steps, across and down, to the tile left of the plus; that tile, the last solid one it stood on, is dug." caption="Walk: the particle (large square) wanders a step at a time (small squares). It digs the last solid tile it stood on before open floor (marked)." /%}

{% figure src="assets/rules/dla-attractor-light.png" dark="assets/rules/dla-attractor-dark.png" alt="The same plus. A particle starts at the right and follows a straight line toward the center. The last solid tile on the line is dug; it touches the plus only at a corner." caption="Attractor: the particle follows a straight line to the center and digs the last solid tile on it. After a diagonal step, that tile touches the cave only at a corner." /%}
{% /part %}

