{% part title="Combinations" %}
None of the talk’s demos runs it with another stage {% own /%}.

- **Erosion:** the talk also uses DLA on a finished map, to wear parts of it away. Its slide calls that DLA for erosion {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s191" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s192" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s193" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-slides/pdf#p21" /%}. See [erosion by aggregation](#dla-erode).
{% /part %}

{% part title="Faithfulness" %}
Our stage against the talk’s own code, each run on seeds 0 to 199 and [measured the same way](#faithfulness-to-the-talks-code) {% own-run values="list.checked.dla" /%}:

- `c05-dla`: 8 of 8 traits consistent with the talk’s own code.
- `c06-dla-attractor`: 8 of 8 traits consistent with the talk’s own code.
- `c07-dla-symmetry`: 8 of 8 traits consistent with the talk’s own code.
{% /part %}

{% /card %}

{% card title="Voronoi cells" id="voronoi" kind="Generator" %}
Scatter seed points and give every tile to its nearest seed: the map falls into cells {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s121" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s122" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s123" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s124" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s125" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s126" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-slides/pdf#p15" /%}.

Stage `voronoi`. The talk’s demo: `c08a-voronoi`.

{% part title="The rule" %}
1. Scatter seed points inside the map’s outer ring. The demo: 16 {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08a-voronoi/src/main.rs#L21-L26" /%}.
2. Every tile joins its nearest seed, by a chosen distance {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08a-voronoi/src/main.rs#L36-L47" /%}.
3. **Edge:** a tile inside the map’s outer ring whose right or lower neighbor belongs to another seed {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08a-voronoi/src/main.rs#L96-L110" /%}.
4. What the edges become:
   - `walls`, the talk’s: the edges are walls {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s136" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s137" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s138" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-slides/pdf#p16" /%};
   - `roads`, our own rule: the edges are floor and the cells solid. A tile is also an edge when its lower-right neighbor belongs to another seed {% own /%}.

{% table label="The demo’s three distances" rowheads=true %}
* Distance
* Measures
* Talk says the edges come out
---
* Pythagoras
* a straight line {% own /%}
* relatively smooth {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s130" /%}
---
* Manhattan
* blocks north plus blocks east {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s131" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s132" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s133" /%}
* sharp-edged, more man-made looking {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s131" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s132" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s133" /%}
---
* Chebyshev
* the larger of across and down {% own /%}
* somewhere between the two {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s134" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s135" /%}
{% /table %}

{% figure src="assets/rules/voronoi-edges-light.png" dark="assets/rules/voronoi-edges-dark.png" alt="Two copies of a patch where two cells meet along a boundary that runs down and to the left. In the first, the edge tiles found by the talk’s test touch each other only at corners. In the second, with the lower-right neighbor also tested, the edge tiles form a staircase joined side to side." caption="Edge tiles (dark centers) where two cells meet. Left, the talk’s test, right and lower neighbors: the edge touches itself only at corners. Right, with the lower-right neighbor too: the edge can be walked." /%}

- **Demo:** draws the edges as `#`, the glyph its shared map code treats as open {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08a-voronoi/src/main.rs#L96-L113" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L54-L65" /%}.
- **Ours:** follows the talk’s words and makes them walls {% own /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="Step-through" %}
{% interactive id="lab" caption="Step through Voronoi cells; Roads (our rule): seed 1, 80 by 50 tiles. Change the seed or a control and the map is built again." params={mode: "card", stage: "voronoi", demos: ["c08a-voronoi", "roads"]} %}
{% steps %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c08a-0001-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c08a-0001-dark.png" alt="Voronoi cells, seed 1: the map at step 1 of 5." key="voronoi.seeds" at=1 of=5 %}
**Scatter:** seed points, at random, inside the map’s outer ring {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08a-voronoi/src/main.rs#L21-L26" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s121" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s122" /%}. Seeds: {% value %}16{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c08a-0002-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c08a-0002-dark.png" alt="Voronoi cells, seed 1: the map at step 2 of 5." key="voronoi.membership.pythagoras" at=2 of=5 %}
**Cells, by straight-line distance:** every tile joins its nearest seed. The edges come out fairly smooth {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08a-voronoi/src/main.rs#L36-L52" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s125" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s126" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s130" /%}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c08a-0003-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c08a-0003-dark.png" alt="Voronoi cells, seed 1: the map at step 3 of 5." key="voronoi.membership.manhattan" at=3 of=5 %}
**Cells, by Manhattan distance:** the blocks across plus the blocks down. The edges turn sharp {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08a-voronoi/src/main.rs#L57-L73" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s131" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s132" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s133" /%}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c08a-0004-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c08a-0004-dark.png" alt="Voronoi cells, seed 1: the map at step 4 of 5." key="voronoi.membership.chebyshev" at=4 of=5 %}
**Cells, by Chebyshev distance:** the talk places the result somewhere between the other two {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08a-voronoi/src/main.rs#L77-L93" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s134" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s135" /%}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c08a-0005-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c08a-0005-dark.png" alt="Voronoi cells, seed 1: the map at step 5 of 5." key="voronoi.walls" at=5 of=5 %}
**Walls:** a tile inside the map’s outer ring becomes a wall when the tile to its right or the tile below it belongs to another seed {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08a-voronoi/src/main.rs#L96-L113" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s137" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s138" /%}. Seeds: {% value %}16{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% /steps %}

On the command line: `map-lab build recipes/c08a-voronoi.json`, `map-lab build recipes/own/voronoi-roads.json`.
{% /interactive %}

Also in the step-through: Roads (our rule). The steps that differ, and its last:

{% steps %}
{% step src="assets/steps/roads-0005-light.png" dark="assets/steps/roads-0005-dark.png" alt="Roads (our rule), seed 1: the map at step 5 of 5." key="voronoi.roads" at=5 of=5 %}
**Roads, our own rule,** for a use the talk describes without code. The edges become road and the cells solid. A tile is road when its right, lower or lower-right neighbor belongs to another seed {% own /%}. Seeds: {% value %}16{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% /steps %}
{% /part %}

{% part title="Controls" %}
- `seeds` (1 to 200; the talk’s: `16`) {% own /%}. Seed points scattered {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08a-voronoi/src/main.rs#L21-L27" /%}.
- `metric` (`pythagoras`, `manhattan`, `chebyshev`; the talk’s: `pythagoras`) {% own /%}. The distance that decides a tile’s nearest seed. The demo shows all three and builds its edges from the straight-line one {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08a-voronoi/src/main.rs#L36-L53" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08a-voronoi/src/main.rs#L57-L73" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08a-voronoi/src/main.rs#L77-L93" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08a-voronoi/src/main.rs#L96-L110" /%}.
- `edges` (`walls`, `roads`; the talk’s: `walls`) {% own /%}. `walls`: the talk’s demo. `roads`: our own rule for the roads the talk describes {% own /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="Measured traits" %}
Seeds 0 to 199, our own runs: the median, then the range 8 of 10 seeds fall in {% own-run values="table.measured.voronoi" /%}.

{% table label="Measured traits: Voronoi cells" rowheads=true key=true %}
* Trait
* Voronoi cells (c08a)
* This map
---
* [Floor share](#our-definitions)
* 0.836, 0.829 to 0.842 {% mark p10=0.829 median=0.836 p90=0.842 unit="seeds" to=1 trait="floor_share" series="c08a-voronoi" /%}
* {% now trait="floor_share" digits=3 /%}
---
* [Regions](#our-definitions)
* 16, 16 to 17 {% mark p10=16 median=16 p90=17 unit="seeds" to=60 trait="regions" series="c08a-voronoi" /%}
* {% now trait="regions" digits=0 /%}
---
* [Dead ends](#our-definitions)
* 15, 12 to 20 {% mark p10=12 median=15 p90=20 unit="seeds" to=140 trait="dead_ends" series="c08a-voronoi" /%}
* {% now trait="dead_ends" digits=0 /%}
---
* [Corridor ratio](#our-definitions)
* 0.005, 0.004 to 0.007 {% mark p10=0.004 median=0.005 p90=0.007 unit="seeds" to=0.4 trait="corridor_ratio" series="c08a-voronoi" /%}
* {% now trait="corridor_ratio" digits=3 /%}
---
* [Path](#our-definitions)
* –
* {% now trait="path" digits=0 /%}
{% /table %}

- **Walls:** seal each cell. 16 regions at the median; the probe finds no path on any of the 200 seeds {% own-run values="c08a.regions.median c08a.path.nulls" /%}.
- **Roads, ours:** 1 region on 181 of 200 seeds, 2 on the other 19 {% own-run values="roads.regions.is1 roads.regions.is2" /%}.
  - **Why the lower-right neighbor:** without it, an edge that runs down and to the left touches itself only at corners. That seals a cell, but can’t be walked {% own /%}.
{% /part %}

