{% part title="Combinations" %}
None of the talk’s demos runs it with another stage {% own /%}.

- **More noise:** in the questions after the talk, its author suggests mixing several noise maps together {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s307" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s308" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s309" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s310" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s311" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s312" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s313" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s314" /%}.
- **Erosion:** its author also suggests running an erosion simulation over the noise {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s322" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s323" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s324" /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="Faithfulness" %}
Our stage against the talk’s own code, each run on seeds 0 to 199 and [measured the same way](#faithfulness-to-the-talks-code) {% own-run values="list.checked.noise" /%}:

- `c10-perlin`: 10 of 10 traits consistent with the talk’s own code.
- `c11-overworld`: 10 of 10 traits consistent with the talk’s own code.
- `c12-noisezoom`: 10 of 10 traits consistent with the talk’s own code.
- `c13-double-noise`: 8 of 8 traits consistent with the talk’s own code.
{% /part %}

{% /card %}

## Shaping and combining

Each changes a map that another stage made, or joins two {% own /%}.

{% card title="Erosion by aggregation" id="dla-erode" kind="Shaping" %}
Start particles on a finished map’s open floor and let each dig the first rock it wanders into, so the map looks more organic and keeps its structure {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08-dla-erosion/src/main.rs#L92-L128" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s191" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s192" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s193" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s194" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s195" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s196" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s197" /%}.

Stage `dla-erode`. The talk’s demo: `c08-dla-erosion`.

{% part title="The rule" %}
1. Start from a finished map. The demo’s: random rooms joined by corridors {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08-dla-erosion/src/main.rs#L21-L83" /%}.
2. **Repeat 500 times** {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08-dla-erosion/src/main.rs#L86" /%}:
   1. start a particle on a random open tile {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08-dla-erosion/src/main.rs#L92-L101" /%};
   2. step it at random until it stands on rock {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08-dla-erosion/src/main.rs#L102-L125" /%};
   3. dig that tile of rock {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08-dla-erosion/src/main.rs#L102-L128" /%}.

- **One tile per particle:** the first rock its walk reaches from inside the open area {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08-dla-erosion/src/main.rs#L86-L128" /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="Step-through" %}
{% interactive id="lab" caption="Step through Rooms, eroded: seed 1, 80 by 50 tiles. Change the seed or a control and the map is built again." params={mode: "card", stage: "dla-erode", demos: ["c08-dla-erosion"]} %}
