{% card title="Combining two maps" id="combine" kind="Shaping" %}
Two maps, each from a pipeline of its own, joined into one: the talk’s point that a map rarely needs just one technique {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s179" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s180" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s181" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s182" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s183" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s184" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s185" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-slides/pdf#p20" /%}.

Stage `combine`. The talk’s demo: `c09-combination`.

{% part title="The rule" %}
1. Build the first input on a map of its own. The demo’s: rooms in subdivided space {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c09-combination/src/main.rs#L41-L79" /%}.
2. Build the second input on a map of its own. The demo’s: cellular automata {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c09-combination/src/main.rs#L82-L114" /%}.
3. Copy the left half of the result from the first map and the right half from the second, column for column. Nothing joins them {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c09-combination/src/main.rs#L100-L114" /%}.

- **Talk’s example:** a fortress on the left that breaks out into an underworld of caves on the right {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s181" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s182" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s183" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s184" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s185" /%}.
- **Then a prefab:** the talk’s author adds a pre-designed section in the middle: fortifications {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s186" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s187" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s188" /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="Step-through" %}
{% interactive id="lab" caption="Step through BSP + caves + spine: seed 1, 80 by 50 tiles. Change the seed or a control and the map is built again." params={mode: "card", stage: "combine", demos: ["c09-combination"]} %}
