{% card title="Placing the exit" id="exit" kind="Analysis" %}
Put the exit near a point you choose, or let a Dijkstra map find the tile that is farthest from the start {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s244" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s245" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s246" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s247" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s248" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s249" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s250" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-slides/pdf#p26" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-slides/pdf#p27" /%}.

Stage `exit`. The talk’s demos: `c18-ending-right`, `c19-ending-dijkstra`.

{% part title="The rule" %}
{% table label="Where the exit goes, by setting" rowheads=true %}
* Setting
* The exit goes on
---
* `right` (c18)
* the open tile nearest the middle of the right edge {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c18-ending-right/src/main.rs#L92-L109" /%}
---
* `farthest` (c19)
* the tile with the largest walking distance from the start, read from a Dijkstra map {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c19-ending-dijkstra/src/main.rs#L92-L101" /%}
{% /table %}

Then the route from the start to the exit is found {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c18-ending-right/src/main.rs#L111" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c19-ending-dijkstra/src/main.rs#L103" /%}.

- **Demo:** the route is the one its library’s A* search returns {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c18-ending-right/src/main.rs#L111" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c19-ending-dijkstra/src/main.rs#L103" /%}.
- **Ours:** always a shortest path; the demo’s [isn’t always](#exit-faithfulness) {% own /%}.

- **Talk says:** `farthest` is the least accessible part of the map, for when you really dislike your player {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s249" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s250" /%}.
- **Talk says:** with a start in the middle, that part is a really bad idea for an exit, and a great way to hide something {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s249" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s250" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s251" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s252" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s253" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s254" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s255" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s256" /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="Step-through" %}
{% interactive id="lab" caption="Step through Caves, exit at right; Caves, exit farthest; Exit without a cull (ours): seed 1, 80 by 50 tiles. Change the seed or a control and the map is built again." params={mode: "card", stage: "exit", demos: ["c18-ending-right", "c19-ending-dijkstra", "nocull"]} %}
{% steps %}
