{% /part %}

{% part title="Faithfulness" %}
Our stage against the talk’s own code, each run on seeds 0 to 199 and [measured the same way](#faithfulness-to-the-talks-code) {% own-run values="list.checked.exit" /%}:

- `c18-ending-right`: 8 of 8 traits consistent with the talk’s own code.
- `c19-ending-dijkstra`: 8 of 8 traits consistent with the talk’s own code.

- **The route:** the talk’s is longer than the shortest walk between its own start and exit on 15 of 200 seeds in `c18`, and on 29 in `c19` {% own-run values="c18.astar.longer c19.astar.longer" /%}.
  - **Why the path trait still agrees:** it counts the shortest walk on both sides {% own /%}.
{% /part %}

{% /card %}

{% card title="The hot path" id="hot-path" kind="Analysis" %}
Everything close to the best route through a map, though not necessarily on it {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s257" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s258" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s259" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s260" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s261" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s262" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-slides/pdf#p28" /%}.

Stage `hot-path`. The talk’s demo: `c20-hot-path`.

{% part title="The rule" %}
1. Find the route from the start to the exit {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c20-hot-path/src/main.rs#L111" /%}.
2. Make a Dijkstra map from every tile of the route at once: a tile’s value is its distance from the route {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c20-hot-path/src/main.rs#L133-L139" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s260" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s261" /%}.
3. **Hot path:** the tiles under a set distance. The demo: 10 {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c20-hot-path/src/main.rs#L133-L144" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s260" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s261" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s262" /%}.
4. **Cull,** optional: tiles at a second distance or farther become wall. The demo: 15 {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c20-hot-path/src/main.rs#L147-L152" /%}.

{% figure src="assets/rules/hot-path-bands-light.png" dark="assets/rules/hot-path-bands-dark.png" alt="A patch of floor crossed by a route that runs along the lower left, turns up, then runs right. Every tile carries its walking distance from the route, from 0 on the route to 6 in the far corner. Tiles at 1 are tinted as the hot path, and tiles at 4 or more are drawn as wall." caption="Each tile’s number is its walking distance from the route (0). Drawn with a hot path under 2 and a cull from 4, where the demo uses 10 and 15: 1 is hot path, 2 and 3 stay floor, 4 and up become wall." /%}

- **Talk says:** everything with a value under, say, 10 is close to the best path, but not necessarily on it {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s261" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s262" /%}.
- **Demo:** culls at 15, so a band of floor survives beyond the hot path it shows {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c20-hot-path/src/main.rs#L131-L154" /%}.
- **The route:** ours is a shortest path; the talk’s A* route [can be longer](#exit-faithfulness). Each side’s hot path follows its own route {% own /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="Step-through" %}
{% interactive id="lab" caption="Step through Caves, hot path cull: seed 1, 80 by 50 tiles. Change the seed or a control and the map is built again." params={mode: "card", stage: "hot-path", demos: ["c20-hot-path"]} %}
{% steps %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c20-0016-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c20-0016-dark.png" alt="Caves, hot path cull, seed 1: the map at step 16 of 18." at=16 of=18 %}
The map before the next step.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c20-0017-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c20-0017-dark.png" alt="Caves, hot path cull, seed 1: the map at step 17 of 18." key="hot-path.marked" at=17 of=18 %}
**Hot path:** a second Dijkstra map starts from every tile of the route at once, so each tile’s value is its distance from the route. Tiles under a set distance, 10 in the demo, are the hot path {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c20-hot-path/src/main.rs#L131-L145" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s260" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s261" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s262" /%}. Radius: {% value %}10{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c20-0018-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c20-0018-dark.png" alt="Caves, hot path cull, seed 1: the map at step 18 of 18." key="hot-path.culled" at=18 of=18 %}
**Cull:** tiles at the cull distance or farther from the route become wall. The talk’s demo culls at 15, wider than the 10 of its hot path {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c20-hot-path/src/main.rs#L131-L154" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s263" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s264" /%}. Cull distance: {% value %}15{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% /steps %}

On the command line: `map-lab build recipes/c20-hot-path.json`.
{% /interactive %}
{% /part %}

{% part title="Controls" %}
- `radius` (1 to 1,000; the talk’s: `10`) {% own /%}. Tiles fewer than this many steps from the route are the hot path {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c20-hot-path/src/main.rs#L131-L145" /%}. The lab’s walk also keeps its caches at least this far from the route {% own /%}.
- `cull` (0 to 1,000; the talk’s: `15`) {% own /%}. Tiles this many steps or more from the route become wall {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c20-hot-path/src/main.rs#L147-L154" /%}. At 0, nothing is culled {% own /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="Measured traits" %}
Seeds 0 to 199, our own runs: the median, then the range 8 of 10 seeds fall in {% own-run values="table.measured.hot-path" /%}.

{% table label="Measured traits: The hot path" rowheads=true key=true %}
* Trait
* Caves, hot path cull (c20)
* This map
---
* [Floor share](#our-definitions)
* 0.311, 0.278 to 0.339 {% mark p10=0.278 median=0.311 p90=0.339 unit="seeds" to=1 trait="floor_share" series="c20-hot-path" /%}
* {% now trait="floor_share" digits=3 /%}
---
* [Regions](#our-definitions)
