{% card title="Hot rooms" id="hot-rooms" kind="Analysis" %}
On a map of rooms, the route says which rooms a player has to pass through and which are optional {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s267" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s268" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s269" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-slides/pdf#p30" /%}.

Stage `hot-rooms`. The talk’s demo: `c21-hot-rooms`.

{% part title="The rule" %}
1. Find the route from the start to the exit {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c21-hot-rooms/src/main.rs#L131" /%}.
2. Test every step of the route against each room, grown by one row {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c21-hot-rooms/src/main.rs#L132-L141" /%}.
   - **In effect,** when the talk’s code is run: a step on any tile of the room except its last column. 0 exceptions among 4,135 rooms on seeds 0 to 199 {% own-run values="talk.c21.notLastColumnRule talk.c21.rooms" /%}.
   - **Why the extra row:** the library’s test skips a rectangle’s last row and last column, but a room is drawn with both. The extra row restores the last row; the last column stays untested {% own /%}.
   - **Ours:** the same test {% own /%}.
3. Highlight the rooms on the route, and gray the rest {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c21-hot-rooms/src/main.rs#L131-L154" /%}.

- **Talk says:** cull the gray rooms for a room-to-room game, or hide bonus things in them {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s269" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s270" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s271" /%}.
- **Talk says:** order a story along the rooms on the route, since the player will probably pass through them in order {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s274" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s275" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s276" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-slides/pdf#p31" /%}.
- **Next in the talk:** a [locked door](#lock), on room five {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s289" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s290" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s291" /%}.
{% /part %}

