## Where the talk and its code differ

- **What this is:** the talk read against the code published with it, one row per difference {% own /%}.
- **Counts:** from the talk’s code, run on seeds 0 to 199 as [the faithfulness check](#faithfulness-to-the-talks-code) runs it {% ref source="this" path="assets/lab/talk-traits.json" lines="1-6" /%}{% ref source="this" path="assets/lab/talk-checks.json" lines="1-6" /%}.
- **The lab follows:** the code. Where ours departs from it, a card or the faithfulness data says so {% own /%}{% ref source="this" path="assets/lab/faithfulness.json" lines="1-6" /%}.

### Disagreements

{% table label="Where the talk and its code disagree" rowheads=true %}
* Technique
* The talk says
* Its code does
---
* [BSP rooms](#bsp): the split
* Divide the map in half, vertically or horizontally at random, and divide each half again, down to room-sized spaces {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s66" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s67" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s68" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s69" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-slides/pdf#p7" /%}
* Cuts a rectangle into four quarters; no direction is chosen {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L86-L112" /%}. Then tries 240 rooms, each in a rectangle picked from all those cut so far {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L41-L54" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L114-L120" /%}
---
* [BSP rooms](#bsp): rejections
* Of its animation: absolutely no rejections {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s70" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s71" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s72" /%}
* Records a frame only for a room that fits {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L41-L55" /%}. Of 240 attempts, 18 place a room at the median {% own-run values="talk.c02.rooms.median" /%}
---
* [BSP rooms](#bsp): spacing
* A gutter of one tile around each space, so rooms don’t join {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s68" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s69" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s70" /%}
* Carves a room only where every tile within 2 of it is still solid {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L45-L49" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L138-L174" /%}. Either way, at least 2 solid tiles separate rooms {% own /%}
---
* [Drunkard’s walk](#drunkard)
* On its slide: place the digger randomly on the solid map {% cite id="wolverson2020-slides/pdf#p11" /%}
* Starts the first digger at the center of the map {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c04-drunkard/src/main.rs#L17-L22" /%}
---
* [Diffusion-limited aggregation](#dla)
* The simple version: pick a random point and a random direction, and shoot a particle {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s103" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s104" /%}
* The simple version’s particle takes one random step at a time {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c05-dla/src/main.rs#L55-L80" /%}. The attractor versions’ particles travel in a line, toward the center {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c06-dla-attractor/src/main.rs#L56-L66" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c07-dla-symmetry/src/main.rs#L56-L67" /%}
---
* [Erosion](#dla-erode)
* Fire particles at a map and blast parts of it away {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s191" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s192" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s193" /%}
* Starts each particle on an open tile and steps it at random until it stands on rock, then digs that tile: the map wears from the inside {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08-dla-erosion/src/main.rs#L92-L128" /%}
---
* [Voronoi cells](#voronoi)
* Find the edges and place walls there {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s136" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s137" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s138" /%}
* Draws the edges as `#`, the glyph its shared map code treats as open {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08a-voronoi/src/main.rs#L96-L113" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L54-L65" /%}
---
* [Noise](#noise): slide 17
* Its left picture is captioned 2 octaves, 0.2 gain, 1.0 lacunarity, 2.0 frequency {% cite id="wolverson2020-slides/pdf#p17" /%}
* None of the 5 calls in `c10-perlin` uses those settings. The right picture’s caption matches the fourth call {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c10-perlin/src/main.rs#L42-L46" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-slides/pdf#p17" /%}
---
* [Noise](#noise): the overworld
* Altitudes from 0 to 0.75 are green, and those above are mountains {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s164" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s165" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s166" /%}
* Draws grass below 0.5 and mountain from 0.5. 0.75 appears only in the water’s color {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c11-overworld/src/main.rs#L31-L44" /%}
---
* [The exit](#exit): its route
* Says he uses A*, but thinks this demo walked a Dijkstra map instead {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s258" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s259" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s260" /%}
* Calls the library’s A* search in all four demos that find a route {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c18-ending-right/src/main.rs#L111" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c19-ending-dijkstra/src/main.rs#L103" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c20-hot-path/src/main.rs#L111" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c21-hot-rooms/src/main.rs#L131" /%}
---
* [The hot path](#hot-path)
* Everything under, say, 10 from the route is the hot path. Cull what is outside it {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s260" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s261" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s262" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s263" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s264" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-slides/pdf#p29" /%}
* Marks tiles under 10 and culls from 15, so a band outside the hot path survives {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c20-hot-path/src/main.rs#L140-L152" /%}
---
* [Hot rooms](#hot-rooms)
* The rooms on the route are yellow, and the rest gray {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s267" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s268" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s269" /%}
* Tests each step of the route against the room grown by one row {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c21-hot-rooms/src/main.rs#L132-L141" /%}. When run, that counts a step on any tile of a room except its last column: 54 rooms on 49 of 200 seeds are crossed by the route and stay gray {% own-run values="talk.c21.crossedGray talk.c21.crossedGraySeeds" /%}
{% /table %}

### Not mentioned in the talk

{% table label="What the talk’s code does that the talk doesn’t mention" rowheads=true %}
* Technique
* Its code does
* What follows
---
* [Random rooms](#rooms): how many
* Stops after 20 attempts, whether or not each placed a room {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L20-L54" /%}
* 13 rooms at the median {% own-run values="talk.c01.rooms.median" /%}
---
* [Random rooms](#rooms), [BSP rooms](#bsp): corridors
* Sorts the rooms by their left edge before joining each to the one before it {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L57-L78" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L57" /%}
* Corridors run from left to right through the rooms, not by the shortest way {% own /%}
---
* [Cellular automata](#cellular): the seed
* Makes its random number generator without a seed {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c03-cellular/src/main.rs#L18" /%}. So do 17 more demos {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L17" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c02-bsprooms/src/main.rs#L39" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c04-drunkard/src/main.rs#L16" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c05-dla/src/main.rs#L16" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c06-dla-attractor/src/main.rs#L16" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c07-dla-symmetry/src/main.rs#L16" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08-dla-erosion/src/main.rs#L17" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08a-voronoi/src/main.rs#L16" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c09-combination/src/main.rs#L38" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c14-not-a-trap/src/main.rs#L17" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c15-still-not-a-trap/src/main.rs#L18" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c16-unreachable/src/main.rs#L18" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c17-starting-left/src/main.rs#L18" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c18-ending-right/src/main.rs#L18" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c19-ending-dijkstra/src/main.rs#L18" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c20-hot-path/src/main.rs#L18" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c21-hot-rooms/src/main.rs#L17" /%}. The 4 noise demos fix their seeds in the code {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c10-perlin/src/main.rs#L13" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c11-overworld/src/main.rs#L57-L58" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c12-noisezoom/src/main.rs#L60" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c13-double-noise/src/main.rs#L71" /%}
* The talk: given the same seed, the same result every time {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s85" /%}. That can’t be tried on these 18 demos as published {% own /%}
---
* [Cellular automata](#cellular): the edge
* Skips the map’s outer ring, as the talk says, so the ring keeps its starting noise {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c03-cellular/src/main.rs#L19-L29" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c03-cellular/src/main.rs#L56-L59" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s79" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s80" /%}
* The map’s edge is not sealed: 45% of the ring is open on the last frame {% own-run values="talk.c03.ringOpen/ringTiles" /%}
---
* [Diffusion-limited aggregation](#dla): the simple version
* Starts a particle on any tile. One that starts on open floor never steps, and digs nothing {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c05-dla/src/main.rs#L49-L55" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c05-dla/src/main.rs#L82" /%}. A particle that digs nothing still gets a frame {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c05-dla/src/main.rs#L43-L84" /%}
* 20% of particles dig nothing {% own-run values="talk.c05.dugNothing/particles" /%}
---
* [Diffusion-limited aggregation](#dla): the other two
* Sends the attractor and symmetric versions’ particles along a line to the center {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c06-dla-attractor/src/main.rs#L56-L66" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c07-dla-symmetry/src/main.rs#L56-L67" /%}
* Neither is one piece: 24 and 25 regions at the median. The talk guarantees only the simple version {% own-run values="talk.c06.regions.median talk.c07.regions.median" /%}
---
* [Noise](#noise): its kind
* Uses fractal simplex noise in all 4 noise demos, the one named `c10-perlin` too {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c10-perlin/src/main.rs#L13-L15" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c11-overworld/src/main.rs#L20-L22" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c12-noisezoom/src/main.rs#L23-L25" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c13-double-noise/src/main.rs#L23-L25" /%}
* The talk names Perlin noise beside simplex {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s146" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s147" /%}. No demo shows Perlin noise {% own /%}
---
* [Noise](#noise): the zoom
* Mixes 3 octaves at a gain of 0.005 {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c12-noisezoom/src/main.rs#L60-L64" /%}
* One octave in practice: with 1 octave in the talk’s library, 0.5% of the first frame’s tiles change band {% own-run values="talk.c12.bandDiffers/tiles" /%}
---
* [Noise](#noise): two layers
* Weights the second noise by 0.75 minus the scale, capped at 0.25 {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c13-double-noise/src/main.rs#L41-L44" /%}
* Zoomed out, at a scale of 1, the second noise is subtracted at a quarter of its strength {% own /%}
---
* [Combining two maps](#combine)
* Runs the cave rule 4 times; the cellular demo runs it 10 times {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c09-combination/src/main.rs#L93-L95" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c03-cellular/src/main.rs#L31-L34" /%}. Copies each half column for column {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c09-combination/src/main.rs#L99-L114" /%}
* Nothing joins the two halves {% own /%}
---
* [Prefabs](#prefab)
* Picks rooms, or spots, at random until the prefab fits {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c14-not-a-trap/src/main.rs#L104-L124" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c15-still-not-a-trap/src/main.rs#L41-L67" /%}
* Never ends when nothing fits: still looking after 10 seconds on 18 and 142 of 200 seeds {% own-run values="c14.unfinished.talk c15.unfinished.talk" /%}
---
* [Culling](#cull)
* Keeps whatever the open tile nearest the center can reach, small or large {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c17-starting-left/src/main.rs#L34-L66" /%}
* A small cave at the center would become the whole map. On these 200 seeds none does: the smallest floor share left is 0.423 {% own-run values="talk.c17.floor_share.min" /%}
---
* [The start](#start)
* Scans every tile and takes the open one nearest the chosen point in a straight line, however far {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c17-starting-left/src/main.rs#L69-L86" /%}
* The talk: look around for a neighboring tile that is open {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s241" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s242" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s243" /%}. The tile found can be far from the point {% own /%}
---
* [The exit](#exit): its route
* Draws the route its library’s A* search returns {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c18-ending-right/src/main.rs#L111-L118" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c19-ending-dijkstra/src/main.rs#L103-L110" /%}
* Not always a shortest one: longer than the shortest walk between the same start and exit on 15 of 200 seeds in `c18`, and on 29 in `c19` {% own-run values="c18.astar.longer c19.astar.longer" /%}. Ours is a shortest path {% own /%}
{% /table %}

## Method

{% callout type="note" title="Our definitions, not the talk’s" %}
The talk doesn’t measure its maps. Each trait, the probe and each failure criterion below is ours, applied the same way to our code and the talk’s {% own /%}.
{% /callout %}

- **What is measured:** each of the talk’s 22 demos, as a recipe {% own /%}.
- **Seeds:** 0 to 199, each built once, by the same core that runs in this page {% own /%}.
- **The data file:** every value, with the recipe and the seed behind it {% ref source="this" path="assets/lab/traits.json" lines="1-6" /%}.
- **Also measured:** our `lock` stage, on 9 pipelines over the same seeds, in a data file of its own {% ref source="this" path="assets/lab/lock.json" lines="1-6" /%}.

### Our definitions

What we measure on a finished map {% own /%}:

{% table label="The traits we measure" rowheads=true %}
* Trait
* Our definition
---
* Floor share
* Walkable tiles over all tiles. Walkable: floor, grass, treasure and traps; not wall, water or mountain.
---
* Regions
* Groups of walkable tiles joined in four directions.
---
* Dead ends
* Walkable tiles with exactly one walkable neighbor of four.
---
* Corridor ratio
* The share of walkable tiles in no 2 x 2 block of walkable tiles: passages one tile wide.
---
* Path
* Steps on the shortest four-way walk from start to exit; null when there is none.
---
* Water
* Water tiles over all tiles.
---
* Grass
* Grass tiles over all tiles.
---
* Mountain
* Mountain tiles over all tiles.
---
* Rooms placed
* Rooms placed, for maps built from rooms; null otherwise.
{% /table %}

- **The probe:** for a map with no start and exit of its own. Its path runs between the open tiles nearest the middle of its left edge and of its right edge {% own /%}.
- **Why those two:** they are where the talk’s demos look for a start and for an exit {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c17-starting-left/src/main.rs#L69-L86" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c18-ending-right/src/main.rs#L92-L109" /%}.

### Failure criteria

A seed fails a demo when its map meets one of these {% own /%}:

{% table label="Failure criteria" rowheads=true %}
* Failure
* Our criterion
---
* No place for the prefab
* A prefab stage found no place for its prefab (the talk’s loop would run forever).
---
* Exit unreachable
* The exit stage’s exit can’t be walked to from the start.
---
* No floor
* A stage needed a walkable tile and the map had none.
---
* A loop hit our cap
* A loop the talk leaves uncapped hit our cap: a particle that never lands, a prefab that never fits.
---
* Not one region
* The walkable tiles form more than one region.
---
* No path
* No walk from start to exit (the map’s own, or the standard probe’s).
---
* Short path
* Start and exit fewer than a quarter of the map’s width apart, in steps.
---
* Few rooms
* A room generator placed fewer than four rooms.
---
* No place for a door
* A lock stage found no tile on the route that, closed, cuts the exit off from the start.
---
* Key behind its door
* A lock stage’s key can’t be reached without passing its own door.
{% /table %}

### The walk

- **Talk says:** hide something at the least accessible point of a map, for a treasure hunt {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s253" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s254" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s255" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s256" /%}.
- **Talk says:** hide bonus things in the gray rooms, the ones its route doesn’t need {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s267" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s268" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s269" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s270" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s271" /%}.
- **Talk says:** a locked door needs its key before it {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s293" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s294" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-slides/pdf#p31" /%}.
- **The lab’s walk:** borrows that, as caches to find on the way to the exit. The talk has no walk, and these rules are ours {% own /%}:
  - **Caches:** up to 5, on floor or grass, at least the hot path’s radius from the route by walking. The first: the tile farthest from the route. Each later one: the tile farthest from those placed, more than 12 steps from them {% own /%}.
  - **Sight:** up to 9 tiles away in straight lines, over tiles that can be walked on, plus the walls that touch what you see. What you have seen stays on the map {% own /%}.
  - **A locked door:** on a level where a `lock` stage placed one. It stays closed, and blocks your view, until you step on the key. Caches keep more than 12 steps from the key {% own /%}.
  - **Afterward:** the lab draws your route over the shortest one, which with a door goes by way of the key, on the map shaded by walking distance from the start {% own /%}.

### Faithfulness to the talk’s code

- **Glyphs in the talk’s code:** `.` is its solid tile and `#` its open one {% own /%}.
  - A new map is all `.` {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L12-L16" /%}.
  - Its pathfinding steps only onto neighbors that are not `.` {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L54-L65" /%}.
- **What we ran:** the talk’s code, with only its window and its random seeding replaced. Every demo, on the same 200 seeds {% own /%}.
- **Why distributions:** its random number generator isn’t ours, so the maps can’t match tile for tile {% own /%}.
- **The test:** for each demo and trait, a two-sample Kolmogorov–Smirnov test. A trait counts as differing when p is under 0.01 {% own /%}.
- **The result:** 182 of 183 compared traits are consistent {% own-run values="faith.consistent faith.compared table.faithfulness" /%}.

